 enough time  in the world for me to introduce myself  as andy new and wander colder if we  hyphenated it number three changing your  name is actually really hard you have to  go to both the Social Security office  and the DMV which are pretty much the  two worst places in the world and then  even after you've done that part in your  name is legally changed then you have to  change your last name on everything  you've ever signed up for in the history  of the internet a lot of places require  a certified copy of your marriage  certificate which costs money and takes  time so it's a huge pain to this day I  still haven't gotten around to changing  my paypal number for women usually love  the idea  my wife's group text with her  bridesmaids had like a lot of heart  emojis and stuff in it  my mom had always kept her birth name so  she was of course in approval a female  friend of mine even gave me her  incredibly helpful checklist of things  to do after she took her husband's last  name but of course I still freaked out a  bunch of stuff number five some men are  definitely weirded out by it generally  men were supportive as well but one of  my friends when I pressed him about it  he admitted that he and I quote would  never  when my wife informed her uncle of the  change he asked if that was even legal  number six the system really isn't set  up for men it was ultimately just as  easy for me to get my name changed as it  would be for a woman but there are these  little things along the way that kind of  remind you how rare what you're doing  really is for example the most popular  name change system is called miss now  mrs. calm this and I'm not mad and I'm  sure it's a great service but it was  just kind of funny to me you don't  really realize how automatic the  thinking is around name changing until  you actually do it  we hired a photobooth company for our  wedding like everybody else in the last  ten years and they provided us with this  really nice scrapbook of 